\ A refcounted vector flows through a compiled word that duplicates the
\ operand slot (dup -> retain), then consumes both copies via native
\ sequence ops (#len, #nth -> native release). Under runtime-image AOT the
\ word body is compiled, so the generated code must retain on duplication
\ and let the natives release, matching interpreter behavior. The check is
\ that the AOT binary reproduces the interpreter's arithmetic result without
\ a use-after-free.

vec-probe: ( v -- n ) [
  dup #len swap 0 #nth +
] ;

V{ 10 20 30 } vec-probe .
